+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales`: body `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }`.
+  Columns may be reordered; ticket is nonempty text, soldAt is an ISO instant
+  with a timezone, dishId identifies a dish, and qty is a positive integer.
+  Returns `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`: distinct newly imported tickets
+  and total portions sold. All rows of a new ticket are imported together;
+  tickets already recorded are skipped. All rows are validated, including
+  skipped tickets. A failed import changes nothing and returns `sales_row`
+  with the physical CSV row number (header is row 1). Consumption follows
+  FEFO, uses soldAt as its timestamp and `sale:<ticket>` as its ledger ref.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD`: returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 1.2, "actual": 1.5, "variance": 0.3 }`,
+  sorted by itemId, for items with positive theoretical or actual use.
+  Dates are inclusive UTC days; from must not follow to. Theoretical use
+  comes from ingredient quantities captured at sale import; actual use
+  includes every consume movement. Variance is actual minus theoretical.
